The legal texts in this repository are Nigerian federal legislation:

  - the Nigeria Data Protection Act, 2023 and the Companies and Allied Matters Act, 2020, as printed and published
    by the Federal Government Printer, Lagos, in supplements to the Official Gazette of the Federal Republic of
    Nigeria (Gazette No. 119 of 1 July 2023; Gazette No. 124 of 10 August 2020);
  - the Constitution of the Federal Republic of Nigeria, 1999, as printed by the Federal Ministry of Justice, Abuja.

The copies used (listed with their sha256 in REPRODUCE.md) state no licence. This repository is private; whether
and how it may be published is the owner's decision.

Changes made by Lexifina: each act was converted to one Markdown file per provision, one paragraph per line;
spacing, quotes and dashes were normalised; the printer's side notes were used as section headings, and Part and
Chapter headings and cross-reference side notes were left out; the versions were arranged as git commits credited
to the laws that made them. The wording of the law was not changed. Neither the Federal Government Printer nor the
Federal Ministry of Justice endorses this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the tools) are
dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
